meta {
  name: replace package
  type: http
  seq: 25
}

put {
  url: {{base_url}}/administrator/packages/:id/
  body: json
  auth: inherit
}

params:path {
  id: 347cde65-90ad-4178-8816-332e19e04748
}

body:json {
  {
    // Required.
    "title_en": "10-Class Package",
    // Required. USD, two decimals.
    "price": "135.00",

    // Optional, but omitting resets to the model default shown.
    "title_es": "",
    "description_en": "10 x 60-minute private lessons. Valid for 3 months.",
    "description_es": "",
    "image_url": "",
    "total_classes": 10,
    "validity_days": 90,
    "is_first_lesson": false,
    "sort_order": 2,
    "active": true,
    // [] means unrestricted -- every active teacher.
    "teachers": []
  }
}

docs {
  ## API explanation
  `PUT` **replaces** the record: any writable field you leave out is reset to its
  default or blank, not left alone. Use `PATCH` (see **update package**) unless you are
  deliberately sending the whole object -- an edit form that omits a field will
  silently wipe it.

  Replacing a package still does not rewrite history -- existing purchases keep
  their frozen `package_data` snapshot and their original price.

  ## API example response
  {
    "id": "347cde65-90ad-4178-8816-332e19e04748",
    "title_en": "10-Class Package",
    "price": "135.00",
    "total_classes": 10,
    "validity_days": 90,
    "active": true,
    "teachers": [],
    "teacher_names": [],
    "lang": "en",
    "updated_at": "2026-09-12T10:20:00.000000-05:00"
  }
}
